# Processor's drift check (#35): does live lag origin/main in code that runs?
# Started hourly by processor-drift.timer; scripts/deploy.sh installs both from the
# release and enables the timer the first time it installs it (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
#
# Compares the live release's REVISION with main on GitHub and checks in to Status's
# co-processor-drift monitor (CannObserv/status#24): ok while live is main, behind only
# in what never runs, or behind in code for 8 h or less; alert past that, and at once
# when live is off main. No check-in when GitHub cannot say, so a long outage ends in
# the monitor going missing. src/processor/drift.py has the rules.
#
# Apart from processor.service on purpose: a Status or GitHub outage costs this unit
# its exit code and nothing else (#35 trap 4).
[Unit]
Description=Processor: does live lag origin/main? Check in to Status
Documentation=https://github.com/CannObserv/processor/blob/main/docs/DEPLOYMENT.md
Wants=network-online.target tailscaled.service
After=network-online.target tailscaled.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=processor
Group=processor
# A release, never a checkout (#2). Its REVISION is what this checks.
WorkingDirectory=/srv/processor/live
ExecStart=/srv/processor/live/.venv/bin/processor drift
# The hard stop. No GitHub call starts past 60 s, but each is bounded per read, not
# in total, then one check-in (10 s per read). Killed here, the run sends nothing:
# silence, never a false ok. No Restart=: the next hour is the retry, and the
# monitor's grace absorbs one missed run.
TimeoutStartSec=90

# No EnvironmentFile=: /etc/processor/.env holds the broker credential, which a drift
# check has no use for. Only the Status key, root 600 on disk, handed over at start.
# SetCredential= is the fallback when the file is missing: the check then runs, logs
# that it has no key, and exits 1.
LoadCredential=status-checkin-key:/etc/processor/status-checkin.key
SetCredential=status-checkin-key:\n

NoNewPrivileges=yes
PrivateTmp=yes
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=yes
